{"chunk_id": "c4b97fdb3700", "text": "Manthara\u2019s manipulation drives Queen Kaikeyi into a calculated fury. Convinced that Rama\u2019s coronation will doom her son Bharata, Kaikeyi swears drastic vows: she will neither eat, drink, adorn herself, nor live if Rama is crowned. Casting aside her ornaments, she collapses on the floor like a fallen celestial being and prepares a scheme. Meanwhile King Dasaratha, joyful after arranging Rama\u2019s installation, goes to share the news with his beloved queen. Passing through the luxurious inner palace, he discovers instead that Kaikeyi has entered the \u201cchamber of wrath.\u201d Shocked, he finds her lying on the ground in disheveled misery. Deeply distressed and blinded by love, the aged king begs to know who offended her and rashly promises to grant any wish\u2014even unjust punishments or rewards\u2014unknowingly giving Kaikeyi the leverage that will soon change the fate of the kingdom.\nKaikeyi feigns distress in the chamber of wrath, and King Dasaratha, deeply worried, begs to know her grievance and promises to grant any wish.\nThemes: manipulation, royal love and attachment, deception and intrigue, power of vows, approaching exile", "vector": [0.005763454828411341, -0.016946937888860703, 0.0030126378405839205, -0.013757485896348953, -0.015641234815120697, 0.015233201906085014, -0.0321529358625412, -0.020211195573210716, -0.012111756019294262, -0.005641045048832893, 0.014417137950658798, 0.005753254052251577, 0.0005997223197482526, 0.02672610990703106, -0.008983508683741093, 0.0011331393616274, 0.058321401476860046, -0.002271379344165325, 0.02344825118780136, -0.02420991100370884, 0.005484632682055235, 0.017422974109649658, -0.007466989103704691, 0.015205999836325645, -0.029895158484578133, -0.0015666736289858818, 0.016334889456629753, -0.030357595533132553, 0.002121767494827509, -0.011241286993026733, -0.00785461999475956, -0.009044713340699673, 0.010887659154832363, -0.014077111147344112, -0.03155449032783508, 0